Your Effect runs twice because React's Strict Mode tests it on purpose. In development, React mounts each component, unmounts it, and then mounts it again. A production build does not do this, so the Effect runs once there.

Strict Mode is a development-only tool that you turn on by wrapping your app in `<StrictMode>`. Vite, Next.js and Create React App all turn it on by default. Look in your entry file (often `main.jsx` or `index.js`) for this:

```jsx
createRoot(document.getElementById('root')).render(
  <StrictMode>
    <App />
  </StrictMode>
);
```

## Why React does this

An Effect often connects to something outside React, such as a server connection, a timer or an event listener. If the Effect has no cleanup function, the connection stays open after the component unmounts. React runs setup, then cleanup, then setup again to bring this bug out early.

In development, React does this when the component first mounts:

1. React runs your Effect's setup code.
2. React runs your cleanup function.
3. React runs your setup code again.

If your cleanup correctly undoes the setup, the user sees no difference between one run and this sequence.

## How to fix it

Don't remove Strict Mode. Return a cleanup function that undoes what the Effect did:

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  const connection = createConnection(roomId);
  connection.connect();
  return () => connection.disconnect(); // cleanup
}, [roomId]);
```

The console now shows connect, disconnect, connect. Only one connection stays open.

To fetch data, ignore the result of the first request:

```jsx
useEffect(() => {
  let ignore = false;
  fetch(`/api/users/${id}`)
    .then(res => res.json())
    .then(data => { if (!ignore) setUser(data); });
  return () => { ignore = true; };
}, [id]);
```

The browser still sends two requests in development. Only the second request's response updates the state.

Some code must run only once per app load, such as initializing an analytics library. Put that code outside the component, at the top level of the module.

If you send me the Effect code, I can tell you which cleanup it needs.

